Reflow the saved cursor with the primary screen behind the alternate

A full-screen program saves the cursor and takes the alternate screen.
Resized while it runs, the primary screen behind it is reflowed as an
inactive buffer, with no cursor moved along with its text -- and the
cursor it returns to on leaving is the saved one, still at the old
coordinates. The shell then went on writing in the middle of another
line: in BeerSSH's test, "typed" after a "$ " prompt landed inside the
wrapped line above it.

Reflow the primary buffer with the saved cursor standing in for its
cursor, and keep where that put it.

--- a/src/screen.c
+++ b/src/screen.c
@@ -1033,7 +1033,22 @@
     screen->sb_buffer = vterm_allocator_malloc(screen->vt, sizeof(VTermScreenCell) * new_cols);
   }
 
-  resize_buffer(screen, 0, new_rows, new_cols, !altscreen_active, fields);
+  if(altscreen_active) {
+    /* The primary buffer is reflowed while a full-screen program has the
+     * alternate one, and the cursor it will come back to is the one that
+     * program saved on entering it. Reflowed with that cursor as its own,
+     * so the position moves with the text it was at: left alone it came
+     * back at the old coordinates, and the shell went on writing in the
+     * middle of another line. */
+    VTermStateFields primary = *fields;
+    primary.pos = screen->state->saved.pos;
+    primary.at_phantom = 0;
+    resize_buffer(screen, 0, new_rows, new_cols, true, &primary);
+    fields->lineinfos[BUFIDX_PRIMARY] = primary.lineinfos[BUFIDX_PRIMARY];
+    screen->state->saved.pos = primary.pos;
+  }
+  else
+    resize_buffer(screen, 0, new_rows, new_cols, true, fields);
   if(screen->buffers[BUFIDX_ALTSCREEN])
     resize_buffer(screen, 1, new_rows, new_cols, altscreen_active, fields);
   else if(new_rows != old_rows) {
